            "text_zhKVeQ": {
              "type": "text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p>Navaratna jewellery is a distinctive ornament style featuring nine gemstones arranged in a specific pattern. The name means “nine gems,” and each gemstone is traditionally associated with cosmic balance and harmony. The concept developed from traditional beliefs that gemstones influence well being and balance when worn together. Artisans craft a metal framework and set nine specific gemstones within the design, usually ruby, pearl, coral, emerald, yellow sapphire, diamond, blue sapphire, hessonite, and cat’s eye. The piece is then polished to enhance brilliance. The colourful combination of gemstones and its symbolic meaning contributed to its growing admiration and recognition as a distinctive jewellery style. Today Navaratna jewellery is worn as rings, necklaces, pendants, and bracelets, often traditional gemstone arrangements with contemporary design.<br/></p>",
                "width": "fit-content",
                "max_width": "narrow",
                "alignment": "left",
                "type_preset": "h4",
