            "text_9btXcQ": {
              "type": "text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p>Polki jewellery originated in India during the Mughal era, with its roots in the royal courts of North India and later flourishing in Jaipur, which became its most renowned center of craftsmanship. It gained early admiration from Jahangir, who was captivated by the natural brilliance of uncut diamonds and treasured Polki ornaments as symbols of imperial beauty and status. Polki uses natural, uncut diamonds that retain their raw form, set carefully with gold foil to enhance their glow and stability. Skilled artisans handcraft each piece with precision, preserving techniques passed down through generations. Its soft, antique sparkle reflects timeless royal charm and heritage. Often chosen for bridal wear and special occasions, Polki jewellery embodies Indian grandeur, artistic excellence, and the enduring legacy of Mughal royalty, making it a treasured heirloom that symbolizes elegance, history, and prestige.</p>",
